# CODEOWNERS — enforcement surfaces
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING IT
#
# This file is ADVISORY TODAY. The branch ruleset has
# `required_approving_review_count = 0`, and CODEOWNERS blocks nothing until a
# review is actually required. It is committed now because:
#
#   1. It makes ownership explicit rather than assumed.
#   2. GitHub surfaces it in the pull request UI, so a change to an enforcement
#      surface is visibly attributed even while unenforced.
#   3. It becomes binding the moment reviews are turned on, with no further work.
#
# A file that states intent and a rule that binds are different things. This is
# the first. Do not cite it as the second.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Why these two paths and no others:
#
#   /.github/**     the gates themselves — every workflow, job, step and check
#   /tools/ci/**    the code the gates execute — the enforcement scripts
#
# Changing either can silently reduce what the repository proves about itself.
# Every other path is guarded by the gates; these two ARE the gates.
#
# Ownership is @Intellora-ai — the repository owner. @sidhutanveer19-code has
# read access only, and CODEOWNERS entries require write access to be valid, so
# it is deliberately not listed here.

# ── Default: no owner ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Deliberately absent. A catch-all owner would make every pull request look
# reviewed-by-policy when only the two paths below actually warrant it.

# ── The gates ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/.github/                @Intellora-ai
/.github/workflows/      @Intellora-ai
/.github/CODEOWNERS      @Intellora-ai

# ── The code the gates run ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
/tools/ci/               @Intellora-ai

# ── The constitution and the locked architecture ─────────────────────────────
# Not required by the audit, included because a silent edit to either is the
# same class of failure: a change to the standard, made by the thing being
# judged against it.
/CLAUDE.md               @Intellora-ai
/docs/SYSTEM_INVARIANTS.md              @Intellora-ai
/docs/FORWARD_DEPENDENCY_INVENTORY.md   @Intellora-ai
